/-!
# Geometry of the actual Rudvalis max4 two-core

The literal core P is special of order 2048, with its center, derived and
Frattini subgroups equal to the marked eight-group under the original
embeddings. Its elementary central quotient has order 256. The actual
max4/O₂(max4) actions on Z(P) and P/Z(P) are the natural and Steinberg
modules, using the same actor equivalence and compatible quotient maps.

Every outside-core involution is two-central, with an actual ambient Sylow
center witness. The full geometry transports to the max4 conjugates used
by Sylow placement. The assembly discharges all structural and fusion
premises of the earlier conditional interfaces, which remain available.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith I.2.2(7), printed pp.412--413, and J.2.6(2),
printed pp.434--435; GLS3 Table 5.3r and pp.291--292.
-/
